---
// A Swiss cheese at 3,800 metres, and what the valley lost round it.
---

<p>
	Here's a fun thing I came across during research: In the 1950s, Swiss dairy experts were sent to Nepal as development aid, and they built a cheese factory in the Langtang valley at 3,800 metres elevation.
</p>
<p>
	So there's alpine-style cheese being made in the middle of nowhere in the Himalayas. So random!
</p>
<p class="milk-story-source">
	Source: <a href="https://www.nepalitimes.com/the-story-of-langtang-cheese" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Nepali Times, The story of Langtang cheese</a>
</p>
